UPDATE public.designers
SET biography = 'Born in Goiânia, Brazil in 1962, Valéria Nascimento grew up immersed in the exuberant landscapes of her homeland — the dense rainforests, rhythmic coastlines and proliferating flora that would later become the defining vocabulary of her work. Trained first as an architect, she graduated in 1985 and relocated to Rio de Janeiro, where a chance encounter with clay redirected the course of her life. Captivated by its limitless plasticity and the infinite expressive range of the medium, she abandoned architecture to devote herself entirely to ceramics.

Nascimento is fascinated by the recurring geometries of the natural world: spirals, waves, petals, leaves and undulating organic forms. Her porcelain sculptures are breathtakingly delicate — whisper-thin, mostly neutral in palette, and composed of hundreds or even thousands of hand-formed ceramic elements that coalesce into immersive, large-scale installations.

Her most monumental work, Rainforest, assembled 10,000 individual porcelain pieces into a sweeping sensory environment. She has created commissions and installations for Chanel, Tiffany & Co. and Escada, among others. Now based in London, she is represented by Woolff Gallery and Ateliers Courbet in New York.'
WHERE slug = 'valeria-nascimento';
